+# Player cue 3 unit consolidation
+
+Tags: #player #cutscenes #matching #unit
+
+Range: `0815AE94–0815C9EC` (end exclusive). The subsystem uses the existing
+`struct Player`; its shared layout stays in `include/player.h`, and vectors use
+`struct SceneVec` from `include/scene_vec.h`. No separate player-cue object or
+header was needed.
+
+The 59 previous single-function files are replaced by `src/player_cue_3.c`, in
+ROM order, with the formerly unmatched `0815C73C` between `PlayerCue_Refresh`
+and `PlayerCue_ReleaseControl`. All 60 functions match the complete 7,000-byte
+range. No assembly placeholders, NONMATCHING drafts, gaps, register pins or
+barriers remain in this unit.
+
+## Shared layout
+
+- `Player.cueTarget` at `0x590`: eight-byte destination copied by WalkTo, MoveTo
+  and RunTo; Motion38To writes its first three halfwords.
+- `Player.cueEffect` at `0x5B8`: address passed to `sub_082315A8`; the precise
+  effect-state interpretation is tentative. The following existing
+  `movementModifierKind` byte selects the sound after a successful effect.
+- `Player.cueOverlayMode` at `0xAE4`: zero disables the overlay; the other two
+  entry points write one or two and update `actionEighteenParameter` at `0xAD6`.
+- All partial `P`, `Q`, `Pos` and `Vec` layouts were removed in favor of the
+  existing shared structs. No offset casts or local layout adaptations were
+  needed in the final source.
+
+## New match and naming
+
+`0815C73C` (608 bytes) is named through the file-local alias
+`#define PlayerCue_UpdateAttachment sub_0815C73C`. The name is provisional:
+its nine-way switch selects the player's descriptor-driven attachment and
+animation. Cases zero through three also play sounds; cases four/five provide
+an embedded counter pointer and a signed-halfword parameter; case eight keeps
+the descriptor and selects animation `0x7F`. The visual meanings of individual
+selections remain tentative. It matched on the first candidate check.
+
+Two old declarations concealed missing arguments. Assembly establishes that
+`PlayerCue_Motion7Variant7` forwards its incoming `w` in r2 to
+`PlayerCue_Motion7Turn`, and `PlayerCue_Motion17` calls `ActorSequence_Begin`
+with r2 zero after clearing heading/side. Explicit three-argument calls match
+both sites, so no function-pointer casts or unprototyped calls are retained.
+Callbacks are consistently declared as taking `struct Player *`. Existing
+`engine.h` declarations are reused; no engine prototype changes were needed.
+
+## Verification and scope
+
+- Per-input exact checks, followed by exact checking of the merged unit:
+  zero differing bytes over all 7,000 bytes; checked again after `make format`.
+- Range coverage: 100%, a gain of 8.686 percentage points; whole-project
+  code coverage increases by 0.025 percentage points (608 newly matched bytes).
+  Existing matched coverage is preserved.
+- Approximately 70 checker invocations, including individual converted inputs,
+  small conversion corrections and merged-unit checks; one new-function
+  candidate iteration. No skipped functions or fuzzy drafts.
+- `tools/merge_unit.py`'s `merge()` implementation produced the consolidated
+  source with no declaration conflicts. Its command-line `--write` wrapper
+  invokes `git rm`, so the caller wrote the returned source and removed the
+  old inputs directly to respect this worker's read-only git metadata.
+- No commits, shared documentation edits, symbol-table edits or generated-file
+  edits. Build products and scratch source are confined to this checkout's
+  ignored `build/` directory.
+
+Full-ROM validation: `build/venv/bin/python tools/build.py` printed
+`build/boktai3.gba: OK`.
+
+Checkout setup surprise: the initial build lacked `build/res/`. Extracted the
+manifest's local resources, then recreated 578 suffixed filenames referenced
+by the shared data assembly directly from their indexed ROM slices (checking
+each hash/index pair). These filenames reflect the shared extraction's prior
+state. No shared `gen/` content or tooling was modified. The completed rebuild
+is byte-identical.
